<body>
  <main class="article wrap">
    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">MultiroomKit / Sonos</p>
      <h1>Sonos authorization</h1>
      <p class="article-summary" id="status" role="status">Reading Sonos's response…</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose" id="result" hidden>
      <p>Sonos returned a short-lived authorization code. Keep it private. Do not paste it into chat, GitHub, or an issue or pull request.</p>
      <p><label for="authorization-code">Authorization code</label><br>
      <textarea class="oauth-response-field" id="authorization-code" rows="3" readonly spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"></textarea></p>
      <p><label for="authorization-state">State (compare with the value from the local authorization request)</label><br>
      <textarea class="oauth-response-field" id="authorization-state" rows="2" readonly spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"></textarea></p>
      <p>This page does not exchange the code for tokens or store it. Use only the local authorization tool once that workflow is ready. Reloading this page clears the displayed values.</p>
    </div>
    <noscript><p>JavaScript is required to display Sonos's response. Do not share the URL, which may contain a private authorization code.</p></noscript>
  </main>
</body>
